  "question": {
    "text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>T&nbsp;</mtext></math>shaped uniform density object with dimensions shown in the figure is lying on a smooth floor. A force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mtext>F</mtext><mo>→</mo></mover></math> is applied at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>P</mtext></math>&nbsp;parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>AB</mtext></math>&nbsp;such that the object has only the translational motion without rotation. Find the location of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>P</mtext></math> with respect to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>C</mtext></math>.<br />\r<style type=\"text/css\"><!--\r\t\t@page { margin: 2cm }\r\t\tP { margin-bottom: 0.21cm }\r\t-->\r</style>\r<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm\"><img alt=\"\" height=\"208\" src=\"assets\\qt0068_826c399d897c.png\" width=\"172\" /></p>\r"
